#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "总览"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:108
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A project model is a means to reduce the communications overhead in a "
"project.  As shown by [crossref:dev-model[brooks,\"Brooks, 1995\"]], "
"increasing the number of project participants increases the communication in "
"the project exponentially.  FreeBSD has during the past few years increased "
"both its mass of active users and committers, and the communication in the "
"project has risen accordingly.  This project model will serve to reduce this "
"overhead by providing an up-to-date description of the project."
msgstr "项目模型是降低项目沟通开销的一种手段。正如 [crossref:dev-model[brooks,\"Brooks, 1995\"]] 所示，项目参与者人数增加时，项目中的沟通量会呈指数级增长。过去几年中，FreeBSD 的活跃用户和提交者人数都在增加，项目中的沟通量也随之上升。本项目模型通过提供项目的最新描述来降低这种开销。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:114
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"During the Core elections in 2002, Mark Murray stated \"I am opposed to a "
"long rule-book, as that satisfies lawyer-tendencies, and is counter to the "
"technocentricity that the project so badly needs.\" [crossref:dev-model[bsd-"
"election2002,\"FreeBSD, 2002B\"]].  This project model is not meant to be a "
"tool to justify creating impositions for developers, but as a tool to "
"facilitate coordination.  It is meant as a description of the project, with "
"an overview of how the different processes are executed.  It is an "
"introduction to how the FreeBSD project works."
msgstr "在 2002 年核心团队选举期间，Mark Murray 表示：“我反对冗长的规则手册，因为那迎合了律师式的倾向，也违背了项目亟需的技术中心主义。”[crossref:dev-model[bsd-election2002,\"FreeBSD, 2002B\"]]。本项目模型并非旨在为给开发者施加限制提供理由，而是作为促进协调的工具。它旨在描述项目，并概述各项流程的执行方式，也是对 FreeBSD 项目运作方式的介绍。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:117
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The FreeBSD project model will be described as of July 1st, 2004.  It is "
"based on the Niels Jørgensen's paper [crossref:dev-model[jorgensen2001,"
"\"Jørgensen, 2001\"]], FreeBSD's official documents, discussions on FreeBSD "
"mailing lists and interviews with developers."
msgstr "本文描述的是截至 2004 年 7 月 1 日的 FreeBSD 项目模型。本文以 Niels Jørgensen 的论文 [crossref:dev-model[jorgensen2001,\"Jørgensen, 2001\"]]、FreeBSD 官方文档、FreeBSD 邮件列表上的讨论以及对开发者的访谈为基础。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:120
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"After providing definitions of terms used, this document will outline the "
"organisational structure (including role descriptions and communication "
"lines), discuss the methodology model and after presenting the tools used "
"for process control, it will present the defined processes.  Finally it will "
"outline major sub-projects of the FreeBSD project."
msgstr "本文首先定义所用术语，然后概述组织结构（包括角色说明和沟通渠道），讨论方法模型，并介绍用于流程控制的工具，随后说明已定义的流程。最后，本文将概述 FreeBSD 项目的主要子项目。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:124
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"[crossref:dev-model[freebsd-developer-handbook,\"FreeBSD, 2002A\"]] Section "
"1.2 and 1.3 give the vision and the architectural guidelines for the "
"project.  The vision is \"To produce the best UNIX-like operating system "
"package possible, with due respect to the original software tools ideology "
"as well as usability, performance and stability.\" The architectural "
"guidelines help determine whether a problem that someone wants to be solved "
"is within the scope of the project"
msgstr "[crossref:dev-model[freebsd-developer-handbook,\"FreeBSD, 2002A\"]] 的第 1.2 和 1.3 节介绍了项目愿景和架构指导原则。项目愿景是：“打造尽可能优秀的类 UNIX 操作系统套件，同时充分尊重原始软件工具理念，以及可用性、性能和稳定性。”架构指导原则有助于判断有人希望解决的问题是否属于项目范围。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:126
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Definitions"
msgstr "定义"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:129
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Activity"
msgstr "活动"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:134
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"An \"activity\" is an element of work performed during the course of a "
"project [crossref:dev-model[ref-pmbok,\"PMI, 2000\"]].  It has an output and "
"leads towards an outcome.  Such an output can either be an input to another "
"activity or a part of the process' delivery."
msgstr "“活动”是项目过程中执行的一项工作 [crossref:dev-model[ref-pmbok,\"PMI, 2000\"]]。活动有产出，并推动实现成果。该产出可以作为另一项活动的输入，也可以成为流程交付物的一部分。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:136
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Process"
msgstr "process (进程)"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:141
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A \"process\" is a series of activities that lead towards a particular "
"outcome.  A process can consist of one or more sub-processes.  An example of "
"a process is software design."
msgstr "“流程”是一系列推动实现特定成果的活动。流程可以由一个或多个子流程组成。软件设计就是一个流程的例子。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:143
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Hat"
msgstr "角色"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:149
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A \"hat\" is synonymous with role.  A hat has certain responsibilities in a "
"process and for the process outcome.  The hat executes activities.  It is "
"well defined what issues the hat should be contacted about by the project "
"members and people outside the project."
msgstr "“角色”与职责相对应。角色在流程中承担特定责任，并对流程成果负责。角色执行各项活动。项目成员和项目外部人员应就哪些问题联系该角色，都有明确规定。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:151
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Outcome"
msgstr "成果"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:159
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"An \"outcome\" is the final output of the process.  This is synonymous with "
"deliverable, that is defined as \"any measurable, tangible, verifiable "
"outcome, result or item that must be produced to complete a project or part "
"of a project.  Often used more narrowly in reference to an external "
"deliverable, which is a deliverable that is subject to approval by the "
"project sponsor or customer\" by [crossref:dev-model[ref-pmbok,\"PMI, "
"2000\"]].  Examples of outcomes are a piece of software, a decision made or "
"a report written."
msgstr "“成果”是流程的最终产出，与交付物同义。[crossref:dev-model[ref-pmbok,\"PMI, 2000\"]] 将交付物定义为“为完成项目或项目的一部分而必须产出的任何可衡量、具体、可验证的成果、结果或项目。该术语通常狭义地指外部交付物，即需要项目发起人或客户批准的交付物”。成果的例子包括一段软件、作出的决定或撰写的报告。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:161
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "FreeBSD"
msgstr "FreeBSD"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:164
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When saying \"FreeBSD\" we will mean the BSD derivative UNIX-like operating "
"system FreeBSD, whereas when saying \"the FreeBSD Project\" we will mean the "
"project organisation."
msgstr "提到“FreeBSD”时，指的是 BSD 衍生的类 UNIX 操作系统 FreeBSD；提到“FreeBSD 项目”时，指的是项目组织。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:166
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Organisational structure"
msgstr "组织结构"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:169
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"While no-one takes ownership of FreeBSD, the FreeBSD organisation is divided "
"into core, committers and contributors and is part of the FreeBSD community "
"that lives around it."
msgstr "虽然没有人拥有 FreeBSD，但 FreeBSD 组织分为核心团队、提交者和贡献者，并属于围绕其形成的 FreeBSD 社区的一部分。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/books/dev-model/_index.adoc:171
#, fuzzy
msgid "The FreeBSD Project's structure (in order of descending authority)"
msgstr "FreeBSD 项目的组织结构（按权限从高到低排列）"

